# `git archive` rewrites the placeholders in any file marked `export-subst`,
# which is the only stamping step a source tarball gets: it carries no `.git`,
# so nothing in it can answer "which commit is this" unless the export writes
# the answer down. fedbrew/_build_info.py is the file that holds the answer and
# tests/test_run_provenance.py exports a real archive and reads it back, so
# losing this line fails the suite rather than silently un-stamping releases.
fedbrew/_build_info.py export-subst
